+## Changed
+
+- Added `src/core/status/queue-pick.ts`, which chooses the queue row to plan: the first eligible row without a slug, or the named row after the not-in-queue, already-has-change, and waiting refusals. It owns the no-eligible message rows too.
+- `prepareQueuePlan` now takes optional `slug`, keeps the active-failure gate first, calls `pickQueueRow`, and then runs the unchanged rejected-item and spend gates.
+- `osq plan --next [slug]` parses an optional queue slug; `PlanCommandOptions.next` is `boolean | string` and is passed through `prepareQueueSelection` into `prepareQueuePlan`.
+- `--run` refuses `--next` whether it is a bare flag or carries a slug, and the remote plan check treats a slug as next mode.
+- Added `tests/queue-plan-slug.test.ts` covering the named-item plan, landed dependencies, every refusal row, the `--run` guard, and a forwarded slug.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- `prepareQueueSelection` accepts the `next` option (`boolean | string`) and derives the slug itself instead of taking a `slug`. This keeps `plan.ts` at the same 249 lines while still passing next mode through the selection helper; `prepareQueuePlan` still takes the optional `slug` as the task requires.
+
+## Missing context
+
+None.
